        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor(qa): migrate Matrix scenarios into QA Lab",
        "body": "Stack 2 of 4. Depends on #101253.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nMatrix QA scenarios and profile selection still live in the legacy `qa-matrix`\nrunner, so QA Lab cannot own or validate the complete Matrix catalog through the\nsame declarative flow system used by other channel drivers.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nMove the Matrix scenario implementations, Docker substrate, and 94-scenario\nparity catalog into QA Lab, with deterministic profile selection and\nmodule-backed YAML flows. Keep `qa-matrix` as a thin CLI/registration shim for\nthe remaining stacked callers; workflow migration and package removal stay in\nsuccessor PRs 3 and 4.\n\n## User Impact\n\nThere is no production messaging behavior change. QA maintainers get one\ncanonical Matrix scenario catalog in QA Lab, while the existing\n`openclaw qa matrix` command and generic live Matrix adapter remain compatible\nduring the stack.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Parity tests cover all 94 legacy scenario ids: 81 module-backed Matrix flows\n  plus 13 intentional mappings to portable QA Lab scenarios.\n- Profile tests preserve the legacy counts and explicit-only exclusions.\n- Blacksmith Testbox focused proof passed 24 files / 232 tests across QA Lab,\n  the compatibility shim, and the plugin SDK runtime surface.\n- The real release-profile command passed 2/2 Docker-backed scenarios on\n  Blacksmith Testbox: `channel-chat-baseline` and\n  `matrix-allowlist-hot-reload`.\n- Exact-head changed-surface proof passed all static guards and the full `tsgo`\n  project build. The two lint diagnostics were fixed and rechecked with focused\n  tests plus zero-warning targeted lint.\n- Fresh autoreview completed clean after the fixes, with no accepted or\n  actionable findings.\n",
        "branch": "dallin/unify-matrix-release-qa-pr2-scenarios",
        "head_sha": "462ddc8705c973775a1c1b163959b166dffede90",
